  "milestone_brief": "Apply the kuzu 0.11.3 close-discipline fix (from milestone adhoc-20260712-955c958) to the 3 residual sites that still use finally: del db. del db does not release kuzu mandatory file lock on Windows because a live kuzu.Connection pins the Database past GC, so a same-process reopen raises \"Could not set lock on file\" (Windows-only; POSIX advisory locks tolerate the overlap). Sites: (1) server/graph_queries.py::cite_neighbors \u2014 live proof-chain MCP library path, async def, highest consequence; (2) ingest/intra_paper_refs.py::ingest \u2014 6th ingest CLI; (3) ops/restore_drill_check.py \u2014 currently no lifecycle management at all. Fix pattern: initialize conn=None before the try; replace finally: del db with a nested close so db.close() always runs even if conn.close() raises. Add a regression test in tests/test_graph_queries.py that calls cite_neighbors twice against the same kuzudb_path in one process and asserts no \"Could not set lock on file\" RuntimeError. Update matching del db teardowns in tests/test_intra_paper_refs.py to explicit-close discipline.",
